WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:09.230
I first heard about Hillsdale on a talk radio
program and got interested in it as a teenager.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:12.730
I already knew that it was going to be a great
place, but it exceeded my expectations in

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:13.730
so many ways.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:17.420
I've got to say that my time at Hillsdale--those
four years were the best four years of my

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:18.420
life.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.420
Just an incredible experience.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:25.260
I went to Hillsdale and I was eager to get
out into the world and change change the world.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:30.270
Dr. Arnn would freely note that I was eager
to make a name for myself and be famous.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:34.180
He reiterated time and again that I need to
study.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.089
I need to focus on becoming a student.

00:00:37.089 --> 00:00:39.739
I became a serious student.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:43.870
Humble enough to really admit that I don't
know everything, that I have a lot more to

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:44.870
learn.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:49.039
I am a State Representative for the twenty-fifth
legislative district in Puyallup, Washington.

00:00:49.039 --> 00:00:51.960
This is my sixth year in the State House of
Representatives.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.690
It's been a great experience getting to know
the community, getting to know a variety of

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:57.690
issues.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.690
I'm constantly learning new things.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.410
One of the very, very important things that
I learned at Hillsdale was the importance

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:02.410
of listening.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.670
That's critical for serving in a public office.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:09.460
And we have to find ways to strengthen our
communities, to leverage the relationships

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.340
that are found within our communities.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:15.500
That is going to take a lot of hard work by
a lot of smart people, much like those who

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:20.140
are coming out of Hillsdale, who are willing
to run for public office, willing to get involved

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.310
in their communities, willing to volunteer
and spend the time and go to the meetings

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:28.710
and do all the other things that take up a
great deal of time, but that are very much

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:32.740
worth it because people have gone before us
and done that in ways that have allowed us

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:34.000
to be here and free.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.240
I want to be a good dad.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.740
I want to do well for my family.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.500
I want to do well for my community.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.520
I was very honored when I was told that I
was getting this award.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.539
And knowing the caliber of some of the others
who have gotten this award, I'm particularly

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:47.539
humbled by it.

00:01:47.539 --> 00:01:50.799
I think, more than anything else, it is a
challenge to me to keep striving.

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:55.920
It is a reminder to me of the principles and
values that Hillsdale stands for, and that

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.789
I ought to stand for in my life.

00:01:57.789 --> 00:01:59.520
Hillsdale is doing a unique thing in the country.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:05.600
And to be associated with that is an incredible
honor and it is something that I hold very

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:05.820
dear.

